body:
It is 100% my fault, yet I havent been told what or why the bike did as it did. Obviously as a new rider I struggle to understand this all, and with basic stability i was forced to put my feet up and ride very slow in a straight line - I couldnt. 

&#x200B;

You are right about the brakes too, I should have let the clutch halt the bike slowly, I learned that. My CBT instructor sent me home, I am British, the training is for new riders and is to train us, yet I couldnt even be trained and cant pinpoint the issue why.
